# System-Level Testing

The `system/` directory contains tests used to verify the operation of the AutoLink RadioSense system using the actual hardware and integrated software components.

Unlike unit tests, system-level tests evaluate multiple components working together under realistic operating conditions. These tests may involve the ESP32 microcontroller, SX1278 LoRa transceiver, firmware modules, wireless communication, and other system components.

## Purpose

The purpose of system-level testing is to verify that the implemented hardware and software operate correctly as an integrated system.

Typical system-level tests may include:

* LoRa module initialization and configuration
* Raw LoRa packet transmission and reception
* ESP32-to-ESP32 LoRa communication
* Packet transmission and reception testing
* Beacon transmission and retrieval
* Neighbour discovery and communication
* Link quality measurements
* Multi-hop communication
* Relay selection and forwarding
* End-to-end communication testing
* Hardware and wireless communication validation

## Organization

System-level tests are organized according to the system functionality being evaluated.

test/
├── unit/
│   └── ...                         # Isolated functions/classes; no complete radio link required
└── system/
    ├── 01_LoRa_Initialization/     
    ├── 02_Raw_Transmission/        
    ├── 03_Raw_Reception/           
    ├── 04_Repeated_Raw_Transmission/
    ├── 05_Raw_Payload_Length/
    ├── 06_Transmission_Interval/
    ├── 07_Long_Duration_Operation/
    ├── 08_Payload_Integrity/
    ├── 09_Distance_PDR/
    ├── 10_Spreading_Factor_Comparison/
    ├── 11_Bandwidth_Comparison/
    ├── 12_Coding_Rate_Comparison/
    ├── 13_Transmit_Power_Comparison/
    ├── 14_Antenna_Orientation_Placement/
    ├── 15_Bidirectional_Communication/
    ├── 16_LOS_Baseline/
    ├── 17_Urban_Built_Up/
    ├── 18_Rural_Vegetation/
    ├── 19_Obstruction_Comparison/
    ├── 20_Static_vs_Moving/
    ├── 21_Channel_Occupancy_Interference/
    ├── 22_Final_Packet_TX_RX/
    ├── 23_Final_Packet_Field_Encoding/
    ├── 24_Final_Packet_Integrity/
    ├── 25_Final_Packet_Boundary_Handling/
    ├── 26_Sustained_Final_Packet/
    └── 27_Raw_vs_Final_Performance/

Additional test categories may be added as the system develops.

## Testing Approach

System-level tests are executed on the actual target hardware and are intended to reproduce the operating conditions of the AutoLink RadioSense system as closely as practical.

Each test should clearly define:

* Test objective
* Required hardware
* Required firmware/software
* Test configuration
* Input or test conditions
* Expected behavior
* Observed results
* Pass/fail outcome

## Hardware Testing

System-level tests may require two or more physical nodes depending on the functionality being evaluated.

For example, a basic LoRa communication test may use:

```text
ESP32 + SX1278                    ESP32 + SX1278
      │                                  │
      │          LoRa RF Link            │
      └───────────────↔──────────────────┘
          Transmitter       Receiver
```

The initial LoRa tests may use simple raw payloads without application-level packet headers or fields. More advanced tests will progressively introduce the packet structures and communication mechanisms defined by the AutoLink RadioSense system.

## Scope

System-level testing verifies the behavior of the integrated system and physical hardware. It complements unit testing by identifying issues that may only appear when multiple components operate together.

The results obtained from system-level testing will be used to validate the functionality, reliability, and communication performance of the AutoLink RadioSense system.
